From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:12:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: restart an OpenAL stream that ran out of queued audio

A streamed sound keeps about 0.7 seconds queued. When one frame took
longer than that (a map load, a hitch), the source played everything it
had and went to AL_STOPPED. The next refill queued new buffers, but
OpenAL does not restart a stopped source, so the music or ambient track
stayed silent until something started it again.

SND_UpdateStreamChannel now plays the source again when it was stopped
before a refill that queued audio. A stream still in its start delay
and one that has ended are left alone. The starved case reproduces on
OpenAL Soft's loopback device. Part of upstream issue 76.
---
 src/sound/snd_driver_openal.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/sound/snd_driver_openal.cpp b/src/sound/snd_driver_openal.cpp
index 7771d989..251f9a76 100644
--- a/src/sound/snd_driver_openal.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/snd_driver_openal.cpp
@@ -1477,7 +1477,12 @@ void __cdecl SND_UpdateStreamChannel(int i, int frametime)
         iassert(alias0);
         iassert(alias1);
         volume = chaninfo->basevolume;
+        ALint stateBefore;
+        alGetSourcei(alGlob.source[i], AL_SOURCE_STATE, &stateBefore);
         bool hasMoreToPlay = SND_FillStreamBuffers(i);
+        // A source that played all it had is stopped, and new buffers do not restart it.
+        if (stateBefore == AL_STOPPED && hasMoreToPlay && !g_snd.chaninfo[i].startDelay)
+            alSourcePlay(alGlob.source[i]);
         ALint state;
         alGetSourcei(alGlob.source[i], AL_SOURCE_STATE, &state);
         bool stillPlaying = g_snd.chaninfo[i].startDelay || hasMoreToPlay || state != AL_STOPPED;
